<section class="py-12 sm:py-16 bg-white border-t border-neutral-200">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <article class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base space-y-6">
      
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-neutral-200 pb-6 mb-8">
        <span class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-800 bg-emerald-50 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full border border-emerald-200">
          Flipkart Seller Hub Guide &bull; 2026 Edition
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 mt-3">
          The Ultimate Flipkart Profit Calculator &amp; Flipkart Seller Calculator: Decoding Fixed Fees, Tier Shipping &amp; Margins
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-2 font-mono">
          Master Flipkart seller deductions, 2% payment collection fees, price slab fixed charges, and net bank settlements.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <p>
        Flipkart remains one of the premier e-commerce destinations in India, commanding massive market share across smartphones, electronics, home decor, and fashion apparel. However, selling successfully on the Flipkart marketplace requires understanding its unique fee architecture. Many sellers rely on raw revenue numbers, only to realize that Flipkart’s fixed closing fees, payment collection charges, and logistics costs consume a major share of operating margins. Using an accurate <strong>flipkart profit calculator</strong> alongside our <a href="/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">free seller profit calculator</a> is crucial for ensuring that every order placed on Flipkart Seller Hub generates a sustainable in-hand profit.
      </p>

      <p>
        Whether you fulfill through Flipkart Non-FBF (direct warehouse dispatch via eKart) or Fulfilled by Flipkart (FBF), our specialized <strong>flipkart seller calculator</strong> provides transparent unit economics. By deploying a calibrated <a href="/selling-price-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">selling price calculator</a>, merchants can determine optimal listing prices that accommodate tier-based courier freight, customer returns, and 18% GST on platform deductions. This guide explains how the <strong>flipkart calculator</strong> works, how Flipkart calculates fee slabs in 2026, and how top sellers protect their cash flow.
      </p>

      <!-- H3: Anatomy of Flipkart Seller Fees -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        How the Flipkart Calculator Breaks Down Marketplace Deductions
      </h3>
      <p>
        Every completed customer order on Flipkart undergoes five distinct deduction stages before the final bank payout is disbursed to the seller:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-neutral-600">
        <li>
          <strong>1. Category Commission Fee (4% to 16%):</strong> Flipkart charges a percentage of the value of the product sold. Commission percentages vary widely: consumer electronics like power banks or earphones may carry 5% to 8%, home furnishings carry 10% to 13%, and fashion clothing can carry 14% to 16% depending on the exact sub-category and selling price tier.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>2. Fixed Fee Slabs (₹13 to ₹52+):</strong> Unlike simple percentage fees, Flipkart imposes a mandatory fixed fee per delivered unit that scales with the product’s selling price:
          <ul class="list-circle pl-5 mt-1 space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <li>Selling price ₹0 – ₹300: ₹13 fixed fee</li>
            <li>Selling price ₹301 – ₹500: ₹16 fixed fee</li>
            <li>Selling price ₹501 – ₹1,000: ₹28 fixed fee</li>
            <li>Selling price ₹1,001 and above: ₹42 to ₹52+ fixed fee</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>3. 2% Payment Collection Fee:</strong> Flipkart charges a flat 2% payment collection fee on all orders (both prepaid credit card/UPI transactions and Cash on Delivery). For low-margin products, this 2% fee represents a significant expense that must be accounted for in your financial models.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>4. Weight &amp; Tier-Based Shipping Fees:</strong> Flipkart Logistics (eKart) prices courier delivery based on the package weight and seller tier (Bronze, Silver, or Gold). Estimate your freight rates accurately using our <a href="/courier-charges-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">courier charges calculator</a> and compare logistics brackets with our <a href="/shipping-cost-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">shipping cost calculator</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>5. 18% GST on Marketplace Fees:</strong> A statutory 18% GST is collected on all service fees charged by Flipkart (commission + fixed fee + collection fee + shipping). Verify tax amounts on our <a href="/gst-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">online GST calculator</a> and recover this 100% as Input Tax Credit using our <a href="/input-tax-credit-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">Input Tax Credit (ITC) calculator</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>6. Statutory Withholdings (TCS &amp; TDS):</strong> Flipkart withholds 0.5% TCS (modeled on our <a href="/tcs-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">e-commerce TCS calculator</a>) and 0.1% TDS (verified via our <a href="/tds-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">Section 194-O TDS calculator</a>) from gross taxable customer receipts.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!-- H3: Real-World Case Study -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        Step-by-Step Unit Economics: Real Flipkart Seller Calculation
      </h3>
      <p>
        Let’s examine a real-world unit economics breakdown using our <strong>flipkart profit calculator</strong> for a kitchen cookware set sold on Flipkart at ₹799 in the Silver seller tier:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="min-w-full text-xs sm:text-sm border border-neutral-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
